# Manual sources (China CDE + Russia GRLS) are not redistributable — see LICENSING.md.
# The archive is hosted out-of-band and downloaded into background/; it must never be committed.
sources/manual-sources.zip
analysis/licensing-risk-2026-08-16.md

# Adverse events are not built or shipped in v2.0.0 (see issues on the MedDRA question).
# Kept ignored so a future PVLens/FAERS run cannot commit MedDRA term text.
kb/adverse_events/

# The external label audit: produced by and licensed as part of
# kevinschaper/drug-disease-compare, so it is fetched (see scripts/audit_regression.py),
# never vendored here.
/fp_audit.json

# The DailyMed ingest intermediates: 271MB and 81MB, regenerated byte-identically by
# `just ingest-dailymed` from data/raw/dailymed/. Tracked until 2026-10-22, when the
# indications file crossed GitHub's 100MB hard limit and made the branch unpushable.
# Consistent with products/ and exports/, which are ignored for the same reason: the build
# is the source of truth, not the artefact (docs/architecture.md). The small
# setid_lookup_report.yaml beside them stays tracked.
kb/indications/dailymed/indications.yaml
kb/indications/dailymed/contraindications.yaml
